# Implementation Plan: Phases 3-6 (Movement, Ball Physics, Hitting, Court Boundaries)

Implement arcade-style player movement, custom per-frame ball physics, contextual space-bar hitting, net collision, and court boundaries using React Three Fiber (`useFrame`) and Three.js math, without external physics engines like Rapier or Cannon.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Court Axis Orientation**:
> - In our 3D court, the net is positioned along the X-axis at **`Z = 0`** (`NET_HEIGHT = 2.24`, `NET_WIDTH = 9.5`).
> - The **Player's court** is at `Z > 0` (`Z = 0.7` near net to `Z = 8.4` back line; `X = -4.0` to `+4.0`).
> - The **Opponent's court** is at `Z < 0` (`Z = -0.7` near net to `Z = -8.4` back line; `X = -4.0` to `+4.0`).
> - **Controls**:
>   - `A` / `D` or `ArrowLeft` / `ArrowRight`: Smooth lateral movement across court width (X-axis).
>   - `W` / `S` or `ArrowUp` / `ArrowDown`: Forward / backward movement across court length (Z-axis).
>   - `Space`: Contextual hit / jump. If within ball hit radius (`<= 1.8m`), smashes the Modak toward the opponent's court over the net; otherwise, triggers a vertical jump (with double-jump prevention).
>   - `R`: Quick reset ball to serve position for easy testing.
> - **Boundary Limits**: Player cannot cross the net (`Z >= 0.7` strictly enforced) or leave the court lines.

